        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pat the tofu dry with kitchen paper. This is very important . wet tofu will spit in hot oil."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat 2 tbsp of oil in a frying pan over medium-high heat. Add the tofu cubes in a single layer. Fry for 3 to 4 minutes per side until golden all over. Remove and set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the remaining oil to the same pan. Fry the shallots and garlic over medium heat for 1 to 2 minutes until softened."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the tomato paste and stir for 30 seconds. Add the chopped tomatoes, fish sauce, and sugar."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Simmer for 5 minutes until the tomatoes have broken down into a sauce. Add a splash of water if the sauce is too thick."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Return the fried tofu to the pan. Stir gently to coat in the sauce. Simmer for 2 more minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the spring onion and stir for 30 seconds. Serve with steamed rice."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The tofu sticks to the pan and breaks apart.",
              "cause": "The tofu was not dry enough before frying.",
              "fix": "Press the tofu block between two plates with a heavy weight for 20 minutes before cutting. This removes excess water."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The tomato sauce tastes acidic and sharp.",
              "cause": "The tomatoes were not cooked long enough to sweeten.",
              "fix": "Add a pinch more sugar and simmer the sauce for a few more minutes. The acidity mellows with cooking time."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "The tofu goes soft and absorbs all the sauce.",
              "cause": "The tofu simmered in the sauce for too long.",
              "fix": "Add the tofu only in the last 2 minutes of cooking. It just needs to heat through and absorb a little sauce."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tofu with tomato sauce is a staple of everyday Vietnamese home cooking. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is often made by students and young people living alone because it is cheap and quick. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The dish is eaten across the country as a meatless protein in a family meal. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "It is popular on Buddhist vegetarian days, when many Vietnamese avoid meat. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Every Vietnamese cook has a slightly different version of this sauce."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
